WEBVTT

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.510
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.520
Kabaddi...

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.410
<i>A low stance...</i>

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.100
<i>A difficult to read center 
of gravity and cant...</i>

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.930
<i>An obscured line of sight...</i>

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.040
He's just like the captain!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.540
Kabaddi.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.790
<i>He's started!</i>

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.800
Kabaddi.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.600
He's quick to decide to evade.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.450
Kabaddi.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.390
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.330
It was a feint?!

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.140
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.140
Makes sense. In that situation, 
the captain would have done the same.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.820
He's traced his style perfectly.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.150
And...

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.040
his expression says he's 
having way too much fun!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.150
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.480
What? He's not going back to his territory?

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.950
<i>That's reckless.</i>

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.450
<i>With this lineup, Sakura's 
got the advantage in build.</i>

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.870
<i>Even if he goes a little wild, 
he might manage to make it back.</i>

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.460
<i>But...</i>

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.210
<i>Masato's counters work 
even when he's on defense.</i>

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.210
All right!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.380
Kabaddi.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.300
Kabaddi!

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.550
What?!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.980
Kouyou, raid successful! 
Two points gained by touches.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.680
Hey!

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.190
That was dangerous, Sakura!

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.960
S-Sorry, Hiro.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.230
I thought he might push for 
the impossible a little,

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.880
given we're talking about Ojo-san.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.240
You were right on the mark.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.460
You really got me.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.110
I was lucky, that's all.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.220
<i>Masato...</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.450
<i>What just happened isn't good.</i>

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.560
<i>This sense of anxiety from having 
the unbeatable ace sent out...</i>

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.710
<i>If this were a tournament, then...</i>

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.600
Yoigoshi-kun?

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.730
When you headed back to your territory,
 you used a spin, right?

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.850
You can use it for stuff 
other than touches, huh?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.230
It was a little different, but spins can 
be used outside of attacking for evasion.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.570
I've built on the things Ojo-san taught me.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.230
That counter...

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.470
When the captain caught you, 
had you already factored that in?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.540
No.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.490
It's just that I'm always...

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.120
trying to think two or three steps 
ahead of my opponents' predictions.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.880
That's all.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.880
The time I spent away from kabaddi makes 
me want to practice all the harder.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.380
You left kabaddi?!

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.720
Yes.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.430
Until the winter of last year.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.260
<i>Someone with the skills to fight 
head-to-head with the captain...</i>

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.890
Were there some kind of 
special circumstances?

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.260
It's not something for casual conversation.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.010
Then, how about if I win the game, 
you tell me about it?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.130
Fine with me. But...

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.340
I don't intend to lose.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.030
Health
and
Long
Life

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.490
<i>Because
\h\h\h\hHe's the Ace</i>

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:44.080
Now, we will begin the game 
between Noukin and Kouyou!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.250
Thank you!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.050
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.050
<b>Noukin</b>

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.140
The raid goes to Kouyou!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.020
<b>Raider
Kouyou / Sakura</b>

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.020
<b>Defense
Noukin 7 Players</b>

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.310
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:55.210
<i>Both of our teams have a first-class raider, 
but our defenses are still unskilled.</i>

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.810
<i>Looks like this will be a fight 
over points during the raids.</i>

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:58.940
Kabaddi.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:00.610
<i>His legs?</i>

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:02.860
Kabaddi.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.380
<i>He's moving wildly! 
He's didn't do that in practice!</i>

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.870
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.270
<i>He's the complete opposite of the captain!</i>

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.360
<i>He swings big, even if it leaves him 
wide open, aiming to get lots of points.</i>

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.380
<i>Since he's so strong, we can't just 
rush in for the tackle.</i>

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.820
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:21.920
<i>I'll run wild.</i>

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.590
<i>How? Did he read me?</i>

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.830
He went in for a catch!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.590
Both legs?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.230
<i>You've still have that habit of Masato's!</i>

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:33.310
Kabaddi!

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.080
<i>In a contest of power...</i>

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.160
<i>I can win!</i>

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.220
<i>I can carry Iura's weight all 
the way back to my territory!</i>

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.070
<i>His follow-up was fast!</i>

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.030
<i>I deliberately showed you different plays before,</i>

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.380
<i>but you won't be intimidated, huh?</i>

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:48.820
<i>In that case...</i>

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.120
That's amazing!

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:57.870
<i>Sakura's spins work as a technique 
to shake off the defense, too!</i>

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.560
<i>My gaze goes from the floor to the wall,</i>

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.280
<i>from the wall to the ceiling,</i>

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.800
<i>then from the ceiling to...</i>

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.280
We lack defensive strength.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.180
Blast it.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.070
Blast it.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.260
Blast it!

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.230
<i>Those eyes...</i>

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.480
<i>These are people who have put in the work!</i>

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.290
K-Kouyou, raid failed!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.790
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.790
<b>Noukin</b>

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.490
All right!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.550
You underestimated our defense, didn't you?

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.220
Not being wary of Date 
and Misumi was a mistake.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.720
You read me?

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:59.710
In sports, the more irritating the opponent, 
the more data you want to gather.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:04.210
The people who irritate me are people 
who don't keep their promises, and...

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.360
geniuses.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.250
Date! Misumi! Nice work as antis!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.160
Sir!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.770
Your abilities took him down.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.700
Do the thing.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.160
At this rate, we'd be better off 
playing against scarecrows!

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.830
You lack muscles!

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.950
Sakura-san was taken out in the first raid.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.840
That must be tough for him.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.350
Health
and
Long
Life

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.370
Let's get back into it! 
We're still in the early stages!

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:40.710
R-Right!

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:45.000
<i>It's because it's still early that he 
shouldn't have been taken out, though.</i>

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.300
<i>We'll keep the momentum here.</i>

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:47.990
Hey.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.870
<i>What a conflicted expression!</i>

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.660
<i>Does he want to go raid?</i>

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>But, he knows that having 
the captain go is better.</i>

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.790
If the raid fails, Sakura-kun will come back.

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.560
So, I can't go?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.550
That one point...

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.620
It wasn't me who sent Sakura-kun out.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.300
Even if they take you out, 
we'll get you back.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:32.090
<b>Raider
Noukin Yoigoshi</b>

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:32.090
<b>Defense
Kouyou 6 Players</b>

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.450
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.450
Here he comes!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.290
<i>Not Ojo-san, huh?</i>

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>But the way this guy moves...</i>

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.740
<i>I've been wondering about 
him since before the game!</i>

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:47.880
<i>He seems reckless, but there's this 
ominous sense that he's honing something.</i>

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:49.090
Kabaddi!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.050
The timing of their catches 
is all over the place!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.340
It looks like it'd be hard to do anything.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.050
Kabaddi!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.810
<i>It's like they're attacking in waves.</i>

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:02.440
<i>It would be easy for a raider 
who relies on power,</i>

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.060
<i>but for the captain or me, it's trouble.</i>

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:09.200
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:08.110
<i>But, man, this guy really is...</i>

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.630
<i>huge and fast!</i>

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.160
<i>It's no fair!</i>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.320
<b>Technique</b>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.320
<b>Reach</b>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.320
<b>Power</b>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.320
<b>Stamina</b>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.320
<b>Speed</b>

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:14.190
<i>Masato-san's exceptional, 
so this guy didn't stand out,</i>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:16.510
<i>but it's like he's totally cheating the system!</i>

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.030
<b>Technique</b>

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.030
<b>Reach</b>

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.030
<b>Power</b>

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.030
<b>Stamina</b>

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.030
<b>Speed</b>

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:22.170
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.130
<i>With Sakura out, this is the perfect chance.</i>

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:25.540
<i>Succeeding or failing in this situation 
will make a huge difference.</i>

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:28.040
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.910
Huh? He's coming back?

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.770
No. He has to cross the baulk line 
or else there's a one point penalty.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:35.450
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.450
He must have something in mind.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:39.300
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.300
<i>What is this guy planning?</i>

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:40.530
Kabaddi.

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.270
<i>I'm going to test a technique.</i>

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.840
<i>Will the move I've spent so much 
time practicing work on these guys?</i>

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.520
Kabaddi.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.180
<i>A weapon that will allow me to 
challenge strong opponents...</i>

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:51.920
<i>Remember how it felt...</i>

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.530
<i>and apply it to kabaddi!</i>

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:54.990
Kabaddi!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.240
Kabaddi.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.240
<i>What's he trying to do?</i>

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.870
<i>A straight-ahead dash?</i>

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.880
Kabaddi.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.150
They've closed off his rear!

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:08.920
Fall back!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:13.420
Kabaddi...

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.920
<i>He's not slowing down!</i>

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.600
He made a right-angle turn 
at full speed?!

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:25.230
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.690
Kabaddi, kabaddi.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.740
Noukin touches! Two points gained!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.690
Two!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.370
It looks like there's no need for me yet.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.850
<i>That was a sharp turn, a cut.</i>

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>Was that the technique 
Yoigoshi's been practicing?</i>

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.570
What the heck was that?

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:52.620
Hey, that was amazing!

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.680
You should look happier!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.670
<i>More than happy... I'm surprised.</i>

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.330
<i>No one's noticed, but...</i>

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:04.940
<i>what I did just now wasn't 
the perfected form.</i>

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.470
<i>There's still one more step beyond that.</i>

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:12.330
<i>He just keeps growing. It's almost scary.</i>

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>For Ojo-san to let him raid... 
That must mean he acknowledges his skill.</i>

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.700
<i>For me, there was just the one person...</i>

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:26.590
<i>And it wasn't acknowledgment I wanted, 
but rather peace of mind...</i>

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:29.470
<i>for my beloved grandma.</i>

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.620
So, you want to become strong?

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.410
Yes.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.410
My grandmother lives with us,
 and she worries about me.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.980
Because I'm timid, 
she asks if I'm being bullied.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:44.640
People around me are always 
worrying about me, too.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.680
But you shouldn't let it bother you.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.640
One day, you'll be strong enough 
that no one will worry about you.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:01.210
<i>Now I have this... I can tell her I'm 
strong and she doesn't have to worry!</i>

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:04.000
Grandma, look! 
I'm a representative for Japan—

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.950
Who... are you?

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.680
<b>Uto</b>

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.680
<b>Today</b>

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.680
<b>Sorry for deciding this on my own.</b>

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.680
<b>I'm quitting kabaddi.</b>

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.680
<b>Read</b>

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.160
<b>Sorry for deciding this on my own.</b>

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.160
<b>I'm quitting kabaddi.</b>

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.160
Read

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:31.540
Hey!

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:37.440
Don't worry! I'll bring you back soon enough.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.820
Keep it up and take them 
all the way to a lona!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.330
Sir!

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:45.660
<b>Raider
Kouyou / Uto</b>

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:45.040
<i>It will be difficult to press in deep.</i>

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:44.390
Kabaddi...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:48.250
<i>In that case, I'll start 
by targeting Masato-san!</i>

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:49.530
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.010
<i>We'll flip things in one go!</i>

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.970
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.120
<i>I'll aim for Yoigoshi!</i>

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.540
<i>It's so easy to tell!</i>

00:12:54.540 --> 00:13:00.400
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.400
<i>Yoigoshi's starting to understand 
the theory of the game.</i>

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.830
<i>Hiro isn't outstanding in any area.</i>

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:07.630
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.320
<i>His strongest area would 
probably be strategy, but...</i>

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:11.310
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:11.310
<i>They've made a chain, huh?</i>

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.920
It's more difficult to stop 
a moving person than you think,

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.060
so it's best to make a chain.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.560
And you have to be careful they 
don't jump over the chain, too.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.360
<i>He taught me that, too!</i>

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:28.490
Practices with the selection 
candidates were always fun.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:34.500
And among them, the one I'd known the 
longest was the most amazing.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.500
<b>Sakura</b>

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.500
<b>Sorry for deciding this on my own.</b>

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.500
<b>I'm quitting kabaddi.</b>

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.400
<i>I'm going to study kabaddi a ton!</i>

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.700
<i>All for the day when Sakura comes back!</i>

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:49.580
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.640
<i>I will bring Sakura back.</i>

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.930
<i>And what I can do to make that happen is...</i>

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:52.850
We've got him!

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:53.850
Kabaddi.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:54.960
He's going over!

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.110
He's going under!

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.060
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.760
<i>You've never seen this play before, have you?</i>

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:12.160
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:14.750
Two points to Kouyou!

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.460
What was that?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.990
That technique is called a Dubki.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:24.710
When I was overseas, I saw tall 
players get taken out by that.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.720
The depth of his knowledge 
is Hiro's greatest weapon.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:32.470
Thank you, Hiro. You saved me again.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.510
Sure. Feel free to worship 
me with all your might.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:38.620
And you always poke fun like that right away.

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:42.480
<i>So, Kouyou's ace is back.</i>

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.710
<i>There aren't many of them,</i>

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.500
<i>but he's a man with the deep knowledge 
and adaptability that comes from talent.</i>

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:53.900
Sakura, you do realize that we can't afford 
to be considerate of these opponents, right?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.600
Yes. I know that better than anyone.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.840
<i>I will surpass my master!</i>

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:07.610
<i>Kouyou will probably come at us</i>

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.470
<i>with a plan designed to prevent 
a huge loss of points.</i>

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:14.600
Focus... Focus...

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.930
Go deeper.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.940
Health
and
Long
Life

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:22.540
Hey, Sakura...

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:26.120
If I don't leave it all outside the court,

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.390
I can't make any good plays.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.610
It's not enough yet. I need to go deeper.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:36.490
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.490
<b>Raider
Noukin / Ojo</b>

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.490
<b>Defense
Kouyou 6 Players</b>

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:38.140
Kabaddi...

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:38.410
<i>That was close!</i>

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:43.120
<i>That's Hiro for you. He can 
react to a certain extent.</i>

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:48.630
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.130
Don't worry about the bonus line!
 Just dodge the touches!

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:48.060
<i>Then, I suppose I'll go take it.</i>

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.240
So that's it! 
They're using the bonus as bait!

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:57.180
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.940
<i>I guess he would be wary of that.</i>

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.160
<i>A feint?!</i>

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.270
He can make it!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.490
This time they used Sakura as bait?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.860
But when they catch him, he can counter!

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.360
<i>A counter...</i>

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.920
<i>It doesn't work?</i>

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:16.580
<i>Masato-san's counters... They're close 
to what you'd find in martial arts.</i>

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.090
<i>They're techniques that use 
our strength against us.</i>

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:21.580
<i>That's why you can't push or pull here.</i>

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.830
<i>I'm not letting go before backup arrives!</i>

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.090
<i>I pulled without thinking!</i>

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:35.890
Kabaddi.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.800
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.970
<i>But he was in the air!</i>

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.940
He used the opponents coming toward him 
in place of the ground to push off.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.270
Sakura!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.400
He got around him!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.900
<i>Ojo-san always exceeds expectations!</i>

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.910
<i>That's why I will do the same!</i>

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:56.560
Kabaddi!

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:58.010
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.510
<i>He dodged?</i>

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.410
Health
and
Long
Life

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.020
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.420
How do they manage to catch him?

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:09.920
<i>Too late! I can make it back!</i>

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.070
Did he make it back with that?

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.490
<i>From this position, I can tell!</i>

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.340
<i>Ojo-san's reach did not make it.</i>

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:31.180
Noukin, raid successful! 
Four points gained by touches!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.530
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.530
<b>Noukin</b>

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.970
You couldn't have made it.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.640
You understand very well.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.650
The normal me wouldn't have made it.

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:46.010
But if I don't look at the line, 
and use my shoulder, too...

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:47.920
my reach goes a little further.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.750
It may be cunning, but I'll 
do everything I can...

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.880
Don't go thinking it will 
be easy to surpass me.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.580
Masato! You...

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.480
Get a chair! And a first aid kit!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.540
We're taking an official time out! 
Please, stop the clock!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.180
How is it?

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:17.700
It's a slight cut.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.280
It isn't deep, so it should 
close quickly, but...

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:24.160
Regardless, until the bleeding stops, 
we can't allow you in the game.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.000
Stay strong. Let's go.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.490
S-Sir!

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:32.610
<i>It's unexpected, but the timing 
isn't bad for putting Seki in.</i>

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.430
<i>He got the troublesome players out for us.</i>

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.200
<i>There are two opponents left.</i>

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.590
<i>We need to use as much time as 
possible and increase our lead.</i>

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.150
Game play resumes! Raid goes to Kouyou!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.480
Referee! Kouyou will take a lona!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.980
What did he just say?

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:52.770
<i>Blast! That strategy was available...</i>

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.640
Take a lona?

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:56.380
You guys don't know what this is, either?

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:57.640
No idea.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.230
That's not surprising. It's a 
right that's hardly ever used.

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:04.650
When two or fewer players 
remain on the court,

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.970
you can declare that you will voluntarily 
take a lona, to have all your players out.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:10.430
<b>(All-out)
Lona</b>

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.250
The other team gains the points 
from the players that remained,

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:15.130
<b>Back in Play</b>

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.130
and you concede an additional two points 
as a penalty for getting wiped out.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.160
Then there's basically 
no merit to it, is there?

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:20.290
On defense, things'll get easier 
because there'll be more players,

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.470
but Kouyou is raiding next.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.970
That's right. There is 
only one point of merit.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:29.560
They can immediately send 
Sakura to raid. That's all.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.250
<i>Eleven to two. We're down by nine.</i>

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.560
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.560
<b>Noukin</b>

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.730
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.410
<i>I've injured someone I respect.</i>

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.180
<i>And I didn't even manage to stop him!</i>

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.830
I went to the trouble of taking a lona 
and you haven't shaken it off yet?

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:51.470
The way Sakura is right now, 
I might be a better choice.

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:55.220
Nope. Me. Should I head out 
and get us back four points?

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.840
No, it isn't that easy!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.970
So, you do understand.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.350
You know that you're the 
strongest of all of us.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:07.160
Why can't you think that 
about other teams, too?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.290
"I'm going to surpass my master!"

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.480
This is the time to make that boast.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.360
Kouyou has the raid!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.440
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:21.340
<i>I ended up going out for the 
raid like it was only natural.</i>

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.530
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.710
<i>Even back when I quit kabaddi...</i>

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:28.740
Health
and
Long
Life

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:33.160
I'm not going to Noukin. 
I'm going somewhere close to home.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.210
I want to be able to visit her every day.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.240
I see.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.720
<b>Saitama Kouyou
High School
Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.970
<i>Hiro wasn't going to come to Kouyou.</i>

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:52.370
That Hiro, I heard he's 
going to start a new club.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:53.980
What's he thinking?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.840
<i>If you were going to go to the 
trouble of forming a kabaddi team...</i>

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:05.370
<i>shouldn't you have just 
gone to Noukin instead?</i>

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.990
I was finally managing to forget!

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.380
Well, that's a lie.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:15.160
No one forgets the matches 
they've been a part of.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.120
Going this far...

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.110
There's something wrong with you, Hiro.

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:22.460
There's nothing wrong with me.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:27.010
When an amazing athlete wants something, 
then you've gotta put in the effort, right?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:31.260
For me, you're that athlete. That's all.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.160
<i>If I return as my feelings compel me to,</i>

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.520
<i>I will be shackled by that 
weight known as "expectations."</i>

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:41.620
<i>But...</i>

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.480
Kabaddi.

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:45.920
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:47.070
<i>A nine-point lead.</i>

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:53.290
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:50.690
<i>The situation is grim for Kouyou.</i>

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:53.290
<i>But... I'm getting a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.290
Kabaddi.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.630
<i>They're heavy, but not painful.</i>

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:03.090
<i>These expectations support me 
when I worry and waver...</i>

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:04.670
<i>They're an anchor!</i>

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:09.610
So slow. Every single time.

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:12.310
<i>Watch me.</i>

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:16.520
<i>Because I am... the ace!</i>

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"The Direction We're Aiming"</b>

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:52.450
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:49.660 --> 00:23:51.900
Next time, "The Direction We're Aiming!"

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:53.270
Kabaddi!
